FINDING (tooling, found 2026-09-01 during Phase-0 gap closure)
tools/check_headers.py --apply silently corrupts a C source whose license
header opens a longer block comment.

MECHANISM: _strip_c_license() handles a block containing BOTH license and
non-license lines by dropping only the license lines. When the copyright
sits on the block OPENER, that drops the '/*' itself; every surviving
' * ...' line then becomes code.

IMPACT: the rewritten file does not compile, AND --check reports it clean,
because the canonical two-line header is present. The gate's own remedy
breaks the file and the gate then certifies the breakage.

OBSERVED: running --apply on this session's three item-18 harness sources
produced:
    verification/v5-audit/item18/thread_stress.c:3:9: error: expected '=',
      ',', ';', 'asm' or '__attribute__' before numeric constant
for all three files, while check_headers --check reported
    OK    571 files checked; canonical header present in all of them

FIX: keep the opener, reduced to a bare '/*', when it is dropped as a
license line but the block has surviving body.

NEGATIVE CONTROL (run both ways):
  fix reverted -> tests/test_headers.py::test_apply_keeps_a_block_comment_openable FAILED
  fix applied  -> same test PASSED
  and the reproduction case compiles only with the fix.
